# Crypto boundary — ADR-007 is a correctness requirement, not future-proofing

`mw-crypto` is the sole crypto boundary. Every crypto operation routes through it.

- Only `mw-crypto` may import primitive crypto crates: `ed25519-dalek`, `x25519-dalek`, `sha2`, `ml-kem`, or any other RustCrypto primitive. Every other crate that needs crypto depends on `mw-crypto`, never on a primitive directly.
- `ml-kem` may appear ONLY under `bin/mw-sim/`, for benchmarking, never on a security path (ADR-006). It must never be imported by any `crates/` library or by mw-agent, mw-ca, mw-control, or mw-cli.
- No fixed-size crypto arrays in wire types. Never `[u8; 32]` or `[u8; 64]` for keys, signatures, or digests in `mw-proto` or any wire/spec struct. Use `Signature { alg, bytes }` and `Digest { alg, bytes }` — each carries an `AlgId`.
- Everything signable carries `signatures: Vec<Signature>` (a list, not a scalar): enables dual-sign migration and threshold signing.
- `mw-crypto` is a dependency sink — it must not depend on any other `mw-*` crate.
- Algorithm capability is bound to attested identity and signed, never asserted in the handshake (ADR-008). Do not add plaintext capability fields to handshake hellos.
- The negotiated `AlgSuite` must be bound into the handshake transcript (downgrade protection).

If a change appears to require crypto outside `mw-crypto`, stop and flag it rather than routing around the boundary.